## 6. A flaky end-to-end pattern next to the robust one
   concept: the same submit, with the server adding no delay, then 1000 ms, in turn (LATENCY_MS=0,1000: a quiet machine, then a busy CI runner). Sleeping 500 ms and reading once passes when the answer is quick and fails when it is slow; a web-first assertion retries until the text appears (up to 5 s), so it passes every time and waits only as long as needed
   $ LATENCY_MS=0,1000 REPORT=.tmp/flaky.json npx playwright test e2e/flaky.spec.ts -g sleeps --repeat-each=6
   |   ✓  1 e2e/flaky.spec.ts:15:1 › flaky: sleeps 500 ms, then reads the status once (1.4s)
   |   ✘  2 e2e/flaky.spec.ts:15:1 › flaky: sleeps 500 ms, then reads the status once (1.4s)
   |   ✓  3 e2e/flaky.spec.ts:15:1 › flaky: sleeps 500 ms, then reads the status once (1.2s)
